    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Guiding you through each stage, from the moment you report your passport missing through to updating your Philippine immigration record</li>
      <li>Reviewing and preparing the required Philippine immigration documentation once your replacement travel document is issued, and handling it on your behalf</li>
      <li>Liaising with the Bureau of Immigration on your behalf, where representation is permitted</li>
      <li>Identifying whether the loss also affects related matters, such as your ACR I-Card, exit clearance requirements, or other documents tied to your stay, so nothing is missed</li>
      <li>Helping you avoid unnecessary delays to your onward travel or current stay</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="context-note">
      <p><strong>Travelling soon?</strong> If you have upcoming travel, tell us your intended departure date when you contact us so we can help organise the relevant steps around your circumstances. Processing times and decisions remain subject to the relevant authorities.</p>
      <p><strong>Does your passport replacement affect another immigration deadline?</strong> If you also have an upcoming extension, departure requirement, status concern or other immigration deadline, tell us at the outset so we can assess the connected requirements together.</p>
